# Line endings. The controller and every container run Linux, so a shell
# script must reach them with LF. With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows
# default) git stores LF in the blob but writes CRLF into the checkout, and
# an SFTP upload of that checkout produced an init script that OpenRC could
# not execute: "Failed executing /etc/init.d/lab-sim: No such file or
# directory" — which reads as a missing file, not a bad byte.
#
# These rules pin the working copy to LF as well, so what is edited is what
# is deployed.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh      text eol=lf
*.initd   text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.go      text eol=lf
*.css     text eol=lf
*.js      text eol=lf
*.html    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf

# Binary assets must not be touched at all.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.gz   binary
*.db   binary
